This project is an independent implementation. Its design draws on ideas from
the following MIT-licensed projects. No source files were copied verbatim; where
an approach is adapted, the original copyright and permission notices apply to
that material.

1. pi-observational-memory-extension
   https://github.com/nik1t7n/pi-observational-memory-extension
   Copyright (c) Nikita (nik1t7n)
   Ideas used: Mastra-style observer/reflector with async buffering, current-task
   and suggested-response state, exact-message recall, duplicate suppression,
   atomic persistence, secret redaction.

2. pi-observational-memory
   https://github.com/amosblomqvist/pi-observational-memory
   Copyright (c) Amos Blomqvist
   Ideas used: fixed token-bounded chunks, observation watermarks, append-only
   lifecycle events, sandboxed structured consolidation, deterministic INDEX.md
   and bounded JOURNEY.md.

3. observational-memory
   https://github.com/intertwine/observational-memory
   Copyright (c) Intertwine
   Ideas used: startup context budgeting, freshness markers, keyword/BM25
   search, source provenance, export and backup.

4. Mastra Observational Memory (@mastra/memory)
   https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra
   Concept of observer/reflector token thresholds and priority-tagged
   observations.

